  "determination": true,
  "rationale": "The `habeas:coverage` citation sits on the `render` method of `Render` in `agent_edge_tools_record_selections_without_validating_targets`. The method only panics, so it is meant to stay unexecuted. The commentary is fenced and gives a substantive reason, which meets the built-in's requirements.\n\nThe explanation agrees with the current source:\n- The test's script calls only `outgoing_edges` and then `submit_result`. Its `validate` calls `ctx.ask::<bool>()` with no node inputs, so nothing needs rendering.\n- The renderer is called in only two places: the content-read tool dispatch in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/agent/tools.rs` (`dispatch`) and the input preparation in `crates/habeas-sdk/src/procedure.rs` (`Ask::execute`). Neither runs in this test, so `render` is not reached. A real rendering here would imply an unwanted content input.\n- The renderer is required by the interface, because the test passes `&agent.renderer` to `with_agent`.\n- Other agent tests, `Renderer` and `DistinctPages` in `crates/habeas-sdk/tests/agent.rs`, render real contents, as the commentary says.\n\nThe citation is on an explicit function with a body, which is a permitted form. The reason is more than difficulty, so there is no gap.",
